WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am very happy
to have you here.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are one of those people
that have been in

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
so many iconic shows
I have loved over the years --

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and films, as well.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.041 size:81% position:41%
However, Peter Gibbons
from "Office Space."

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.211
You are approached about this
character a great deal, I hear.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:14.180
-That's probably the one, yeah,
that I get hit with the most.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And people actually
have told you

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
that character
is inspiring to them.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.286
-Yeah. I mean, people will
come up to me from time to time

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.223
and say, you know, "This movie
and you were the reason that I

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
quit my job and walked away
from my livelihood."

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.629 line:92%
-And I'm always a little --

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wait five seconds before
I say, "Good for you,"

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I don't know
which way it went.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, yeah,
it's usually good or they

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.306
wouldn't they'd have just
taken me out from behind.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, so, you're also
on "Sex and the City."

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You were Berger.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I was Berger.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.948 line:92%
-And you had one of the great

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody recognized
you as Berger of all time.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:55.121
I feel like being in that show,
having a part in that show,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
explain who recognized you
at a Lakers game.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was so surreal.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
The agency I was with
at the time

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.263 line:92%
had courtside Laker tickets.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:07.133
And, for some reason, everyone
else must have been out of town,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.701 line:92%
'cause I got the invite to go.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, at some point during
the second quarter,

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.839 line:92%
there was a ball out of bounds,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Kobe came over
on the in-bound.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:20.413
And he looked at me and did a
double take and said, "Berger?"

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Wow!"
-That's really great.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I'll always have that.
-You'll always have that.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was mentioning
to you, backstage,

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.157 line:92%
I've never seen the show.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.526
My wife's making me watch it.
I'm enjoying it a great deal.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.627 line:92%
I haven't come to Berger yet.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I won't spoil it.
-Okay, great.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will I --
After I see the Berger arc,

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:39.933 line:92%
will I think, "Man, Carrie --

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wish Carrie had
ended up with Berger"?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.004
-Only if you have a really
messed-up idea of relationships.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.406 line:92%
-Okay, gotcha. Well, we'll see.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll see when
that moment comes.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:51.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a 5-year-old, yes?
-I do.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.913
I have a 5-year-old and a
2-year-old, who's about to be 3.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you are -- you're raising
them in L.A., obviously.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.186
-How is --
Obviously, you have a new show.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:00.887 size:75% position:38% line:92%
You have billboards.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:04.057
Your face is on while
they're driving down the street.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.791 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How is that for them?

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.260
-It's kind of -- Well, first of
all, I think kids today --

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.196 size:84% position:42%
it's not quite so weird
to see people on TV,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they see
themselves on TV.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody can,
you know, shoot everything.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.069 size:84% position:42%
But the billboards are
a little bit different.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.938 size:84% position:42%
And, you know, the kids
kind of respond to it.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it is L.A.,
so, you know, a couple of

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
the other preschool dads
were saying,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.278 line:92%
"Yeah, my kid came and said,

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:28.014
'Daddy, when are
you going to be on a billboard?

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.749 line:92%
I've seen three of them already

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
of other parents
in the school.'"

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is, yeah,
raising a very unfair bar.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's
great values, great values.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.694
-So, this new show -- I don't
want to give too much away,

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this is something
that has been in

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
the trailers and
the promotion of the show.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.401
Your character commits suicide.
-Yes.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.938
-And this is -- You are still in
the show, from flashbacks.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What made you choose
to do a show

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
where your character so
immediately dies?

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.680 line:92%
-Well, my first thought was,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm old enough to remember
'The Big Chill.'"

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "It worked out
for Kevin Costner."

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jackpot for Costner.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:11.090
And he didn't even say anything.
-Yeah. He was, like, in and out.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right?
-He had like two days work.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:16.262 line:92%
-Now he's dancing with wolves.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.830 line:92%
So I felt pretty good about it.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's also --
I'm doing another show,

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.434 size:75% position:38%
on Audience network,
called "Loudermilk."

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.470
It's Season 2 of doing that.
That's kind of my day gig.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.974
-So, this one -- it sort of had
to be a limited thing

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
or it just wouldn't have been
able to happen.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-So it was great.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you in --
How far into the process of

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Season 2 are you
on "Loudermilk" now?

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:37.884
-I think "Loudermilk" --
we've shot all 10 of them.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
And "A Million Little Things,"
we're up to,

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.589 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I think, 106 or 107.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And "Loudermilk" is --
For who don't know,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:48.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is another
sort of complicated character.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
Explain that character
a little bit.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what made you
want to do that one?

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's basically the
biggest A-hole in the world.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-I can say that, yeah.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you can say that.
-Okay.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You could say
the whole word, if you want.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Go for it.
Try it. See how it feels.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no. I'm not gonna do it.
-Okay.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.508 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I don't want the fine.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.677
-That shows how different
you are than "Loudermilk"

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.412 line:92%
that you won't even say it.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, you know,
he's sort of, like,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
this deadbeat,
you know, misanthrope,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.288 line:92%
who's a recovery counselor,

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
a substance-abuse recovery
counselor

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
for this group of
misfits and numbskulls.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just classic,
you know, comedy.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:26.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the Farrelly brothers.
Will Sasso is on it.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a blast to do.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- Obviously,
you're working with

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
great television-makers,
great filmmakers.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.274 line:92%
Matt Weiner -- "Mad Men" --

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
has a new show called
"The Romanoffs."

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You're in that, as well.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:37.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is a show --
very inscrutable trailer.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very hard to tell
what the show is about.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can you understand
what it's about?

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:46.352
-No. I was in it and I have
no idea what it was about.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:46.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're confident we'll
all like it?

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I am.

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think because Matt's
a mad genius,

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.626
but he is one of those guys
that just likes everything

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:57.130
to be secret so that it can,
you know, do the whole thing.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I respect that.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's an anthology -- Well,
I don't know.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think it's an --

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
All I know is --
I'm in only in one of them,

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I assume -- I hope everyone
else is not in all of them,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm the only --
I don't know.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
My fingers are crossed
that you find out.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, everybody but Ron's
in all of them."

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
I'll be like, "Oh, gosh."

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
I looked really dumb on
"Seth Meyers."

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.590 line:92%
-You're not from Chicago,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you lived
there after college?

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:29.696
-And what brought you to
Chicago in the first place?

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know what?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.898
It was just one of those things
where I got out of school

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was kind of
floating around.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew I was going to give
acting a shot somewhere.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:40.840
I was probably too chicken
to come and try it in New York.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought about Seattle
for a minute,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:43.609 line:92%
because I didn't really know

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:46.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
the difference between
acting and music.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then sort of
decided on Chicago

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.984
because it was close to home
and Steppenwolf was a big deal.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.353
-Sure.
-You know, had been a big deal.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.021 line:92%
So we were all chasing that.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first time I saw you
was in "Swingers."

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you meet those guys
in Chicago?

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:00.393 line:92%
Did you meet Favreau there?

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:03.396 size:78% position:39%
-I met Jon in Chicago
and I met Vince --

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:06.733 size:84% position:42%
Jon and I moved to L.A.
at about the same time

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:10.303
and became closer friends
sort of by the fact that

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:13.606
we were the only two people that
moved to L.A. in that month,

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.908 line:92%
and so we only knew each other.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:20.480
But he knew Vince from doing
"Rudy" earlier, the two of them.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.048 line:92%
And they -- I mean, it's kind of

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:25.251
a documentary, "Swingers,"
really, of what it was like

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be 26 in L.A.,
starting out as an actor.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:31.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you know,
obviously, one of the legend

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
of that movie is,
you know, you guys couldn't

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
possibly have known
you were making this film

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:35.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was going to,
again, like, sort of

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
be this indelible mark on
that moment in time,

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:38.865 size:81% position:41% line:92%
which it certainly is.

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have any sense that
it was going to be

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.168
a film that people were gong to
see and remember for this long?

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.036 size:75% position:38%
-No. We didn't think
it was going to be

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:44.704 size:88% position:44% line:92%
a movie that we were in.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
We rehearsed --
We did readings of it

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
for like a year,
trying to help Jon sell it,

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:51.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the idea that, "Well,
we're never going to be in it,

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.413 size:84% position:42%
but maybe some producer
will see us," you know?

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:53.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:56.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then it just worked out
that we got to do it.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:59.652
And it's, you know, lightning in
a bottle, one of those.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.987 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah. A fantastic film.

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was living
in Chicago at the time,

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was so cool to us that
like, "Oh, my God.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those guys who lived here
went to L.A. and made a movie,

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now everybody's
talking about it and stuff."

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.529
-Right.
"What are we doing in Chicago?"

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:10.329 line:92%
-Yeah. "We've got to get to L.A.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
and do one of those
producer tables."

